    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/senior-lecturer-medical-coordinator-kalgoorlie-crawley-wa-australia-kalgoorlie": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer (Medical Coordinator) - Kalgoorlie",
      "description": "Senior Lecturer (Medical Coordinator) - Kalgoorlie - Crawley, WA, Australia - Kalgoorlie, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Senior Lecturer (Medical Coordinator) - Kalgoorlie 521790 Crawley, WA Kalgoorlie, WA Part Time Closing on: 8 Nov 2026 UWA Medical School Rural Clinical School of WA (RCSWA) Based in Kalgoorlie in Regional Western Australia Become a key part of transforming lives and improving health outcomes in rural communities Part-time (0.4FTE or 2 x 0.2FTE considered) appointment on a fixed term basis until December 2026 (with anticipated extension to December 2031) Base salary range: Level C, $149,909 – $172,441 p.a. (pro-rata) plus 17% superannuation. Rural and remote allowance applies for those living in the immediate area Clinical loading applicable About the area The Rural Clinical School of Western Australia (RCSWA) was established in 2002 to help deliver better health outcomes for people living in country WA. Our vision for the future is to build on our successes and foster an exceptional locally trained, research-driven, collegiate, academic and clinical community, providing equitable healthcare to rural and remote WA. The RCSWA helps rural communities sustain a locally trained and loyal medical workforce by placing penultimate and final year medical students across a network of 15 sites. Students gain valuable hands-on experience and professional mentoring throughout the 12-month program. About the opportunity Deliver world-class innovative medical education and training to medical students and assist in the support of preceptors and host practitioners Commitment to be involved in research and/or evaluation relevant to improving rural health In consultation with local medical practitioners and agencies maintain and contribute to the development of local educational programs that meet the requirements of the RCSWA and take advantage of local opportunities and strengths Develop and coordinate the development of rural training pathways in local area of appointment and contribute to a statewide RCSWA approach About you Registered, or able to be registered with AHPRA as a Medical Practitioner Committed to working in medical practice in rural WA Available to work in the respective RCSWA site and the ability to network with rural practitioners in the region Experience as a preceptor and/or supervisor of medical students and/or junior doctors or registrars A commitment to the principles and practice of Indigenous health in rural and regional areas Commitment to rural medical education and to improving rural medical workforce Position description: POSITION DESCRIPTION - [Senior Lecturer (Medical Coordinator)] - Level [C].docx To learn more about this opportunity, please contact Robyn Fortune at robyn.fortune@rcswa.edu.au How to apply Please apply online via the Apply Now button and address the selection criteria in your submission in a separate document. For information to assist you with compiling statements to answer the selection criteria, please visit Addressing the selection criteria . You may submit a statement describing any personal circumstances relevant to your application. This can include academic/professional interruptions or achievements relative to opportunity. Closing date: 11:55 PM AWST on Sunday, 8 November 2026 This position is only open to applicants with relevant rights to work in Australia About the University The University of Western Australia (UWA) is ranked among the top 100 universities in the world and a member of the prestigious Australian Group of Eight research intensive universities. With a strong research track record, vibrant campus and working environments, supported by the freedom to innovate and inspire, there is no better time to join Western Australia’s top university. Learn more about us. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity UWA is committed to a diverse workforce and an equitable and inclusive workplace. We are committed to fostering a safe environment for all, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, women, those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, the LGBTIQA+ community, and people living with disability. If you require any reasonable adjustments, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application. Alternatively, you can contact us for assistance during the recruitment process. If you have queries relating to your application, please contact the individual named in the advertisement. Alternatively, please contact the Talent team at people@uwa.edu.au with details of your query. To enable a quick response, please include the 6-digit job reference number. Back to job search Other jobs Casual – Tutors (Business School) Crawley, WA Business Join UWA Business School as a casual tutor in Semester 1, 2027 and gain valuable teaching experience with flexible hours and competitive rates Scholarship Officer Crawley, WA Student Administration / Support Services Coordinate scholarship applications, awards and administration while providing clear advice to students and stakeholders. Academic Services Officer - Kalogoorlie Kalgoorlie, WA Administration & Executive support Join a collaborative team supporting the education and development of the next generation of rural doctors in Western Australia. Benefits Flexible working options considered. 26 weeks paid parental leave after one year and 36 weeks after five years continuous service, regardless of gender. 4 weeks annual leave with the option to purchase more. 13 weeks long service leave after seven/ten years. Salary packaging options. 17% superannuation, with the option to reduce to the minimum super guarantee. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance, and convenient on-campus childcare options. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Excluding casual positions. The University of Western Australia acknowledges that its campus is situated on Noongar land, and that Noongar people remain the spiritual and cultural custodians of their land, and continue to practise their values, languages, beliefs and knowledge. Indigenous commitment Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X Youtube Cookie Preferences Privacy Policy © 2026 The University of Western Australia Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
    },
    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/lecturer-archaeology-crawley-wa-australia": {
      "title": "Lecturer - Archaeology",
      "description": "Lecturer - Archaeology - Crawley, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Lecturer - Archaeology 524764 Crawley, WA Full Time Closing on: 4 Dec 2026 Shape the next generation through innovative teaching in Australian Archaeology. First Nations applicants are encouraged to apply. Full-time appointment on a fixed term basis for 4 years commencing in June 2027. Base salary range: Level B, $122,876 – $145,404 p.a. (pro-rata) plus 17% superannuation. About the area The School of Social Sciences provides a rich teaching and research environment across disciplinary and interdisciplinary areas in the applied social sciences. It delivers undergraduate and postgraduate programs and supports an active research program. Archaeology is a research flagship within the School, bringing together globally visible researchers, networks and an award-winning teaching program focused on Australian Archaeology. Western Australia offers exceptional opportunities to work with communities of interest, pursue globally significant archaeological research and help meet strong demand for skilled practitioners. About the opportunity Deliver engaging undergraduate teaching in Australian Archaeology, including laboratory and field-based learning, while contributing to curriculum development, assessment design and an outstanding student experience. Supervise undergraduate, Honours, Masters and PhD students and support fieldwork, placements and other learning opportunities that strengthen graduate employability. Strengthen student experience and graduate employability while contributing to the collegial life, governance and external engagement of the School and University. About you A PhD in Archaeology, a relevant academic field, or an appropriate higher professional qualification. Demonstrated expertise in Australian Archaeology, with the capacity to teach Australian archaeology units and deliver high-quality laboratory and field-based learning. A commitment to inclusive, research-led teaching, contemporary assessment and the effective use of technology, together with a collaborative approach to curriculum development and delivery. Experience contributing to curriculum development and using contemporary teaching approaches and technology to enhance student learning. Experience in one or more of Indigenous Archaeology, Archaeological Science, or Historical and Maritime Archaeology, with the ability to supervise research students, pursue external funding and engage effectively with community, government, industry and university partners. Note : As part of the recruitment process, candidates will be required to complete declarations in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence. A current National Police Clearance will be required by the successful applicant. Position description: PD - Lecturer Archeology (524764).pdf To learn more about this opportunity, please contact Professor Amanda Davies at amanda.davies@uwa.edu.au For enquiries on the recruitment process, please contact Maddy Chaplin at maddy.chaplin@uwa.edu.au How to apply Please apply online via the Apply Now button and address the selection criteria in your submission in a separate document. For information to assist you with compiling statements to answer the selection criteria, please visit Addressing the selection criteria . You may submit a statement describing any personal circumstances relevant to your application. This can include academic/professional interruptions or achievements relative to opportunity. Closing date: 11:55 PM AWST on Friday, 4 December 2026. This position is open to international applicants. Benefits Flexible working options. Generous paid leave including parental leave. Up to 17% employer paid superannuation. Salary packaging available. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance. Employee Assistance Program. About the University The University of Western Australia (UWA) is ranked among the top 100 universities in the world and a member of the prestigious Australian Group of Eight research intensive universities. With a strong research track record, vibrant campus and working environments, supported by the freedom to innovate and inspire, there is no better time to join Western Australia’s top university. Learn more about us. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity UWA is committed to a diverse workforce and an equitable and inclusive workplace. We are committed to fostering a safe environment for all, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, women, those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, the LGBTIQA+ community, and people living with disability. If you require any reasonable adjustments, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application. Alternatively, you can contact us for assistance during the recruitment process. If you have queries relating to your application, please contact the individual named in the advertisement. To enable a quick response, please include the 6-digit job reference number. Other jobs Systems Engineer Crawley, WA Research support, Technical/Laboratory support Design and deliver critical systems for the SKA telescope, collaborating with global experts to advance world-leading astronomy and photonics engineering Helpdesk Support Assistant Crawley, WA Campus / facilities management Play a critical role as the first point of contact in a fast-paced facilities and maintenance environment. Senior Lecturer  - Regional Training Hubs (based in Broome, Derby or Kununurra) Any RCSWA site, WA. Broome, WA Health and Medical Sciences Play a key leadership role in strengthening rural medical education and training pathways across regional and remote Western Australia. Benefits Flexible working options considered. 26 weeks paid parental leave after one year and 36 weeks after five years continuous service, regardless of gender. 4 weeks annual leave with the option to purchase more. 13 weeks long service leave after seven/ten years. Salary packaging options. 17% superannuation, with the option to reduce to the minimum super guarantee. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance, and convenient on-campus childcare options. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Excluding casual positions. The University of Western Australia acknowledges that its campus is situated on Noongar land, and that Noongar people remain the spiritual and cultural custodians of their land, and continue to practise their values, languages, beliefs and knowledge. Indigenous commitment Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X Youtube Cookie Preferences Privacy Policy © 2026 The University of Western Australia Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
    },
    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/systems-engineer-crawley-wa-australia": {
      "title": "Systems Engineer",
      "description": "Systems Engineer - Crawley, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Systems Engineer 524859 Crawley, WA Full Time Closing on: 22 Nov 2026 Join a globally significant science and engineering project helping to deliver the world's largest radio telescope, the Square Kilometre Array (SKA). Apply your systems engineering expertise to advanced optical fibre, frequency transfer and astronomical instrumentation technologies in a highly collaborative international environment. Full-time (1 FTE) appointment on a fixed term basis for 12 months. Base salary range: $120,912 – $132,161 p.a. plus 17% superannuation. About the area The International Centre for Radio Astronomy Research (ICRAR) is a high-profile joint venture between The University of Western Australia and Curtin University. Established in 2009 and supported by the Western Australian Government, ICRAR is one of Australia’s leading astronomy organisations and a key contributor to the international Square Kilometre Array (SKA) Project. Within ICRAR, the Astrophotonics Group designs, builds and tests advanced photonic systems for radio astronomy, optical astronomy and space science. The group brings together expertise in astronomy, physics and engineering, with core capability in the long-distance transfer of stabilised optical-frequency, microwave-frequency and timing signals across optical fibre networks and free-space laser links. About the opportunity Support the Design Authority, Systems Engineering Manager and Senior Systems Engineer, to develop and refine the architecture, requirements, interfaces and design baselines for the SKA-Mid Frequency Distribution System, in line with SKAO requirements, standards and the Systems Engineering Management Plan. Lead and contribute to requirements engineering, trade studies, risk and RAMS analyses, FMEA, configuration and change control, and verification and validation planning; produce high-quality specifications, interface control documents, test procedures and configuration records. Work across office-based engineering and hands-on laboratory integration and testing, collaborating with SKAO, partner institutions, industry, quality and engineering teams to resolve complex technical issues and deliver compliant project outcomes. About you A tertiary qualification in systems engineering, electrical engineering or a related discipline, together with extensive relevant experience, or equivalent demonstrated professional experience. Extensive experience applying systems engineering and lifecycle principles to complex technical systems, including architecture, requirements management, interface management, integration, verification and validation, risk analysis, and engineering change control. Experience in RAMS analysis and FMEA, with strong analytical capability and a track record of identifying technical risks early and developing practical mitigations. Proficiency with system modelling tools such as Cameo Systems Modeler (SysML) and/or Microsoft Visio, and experience using a requirements management platform such as JAMA. Hands-on laboratory or field experience in system integration, testing and technical verification, supported by clear technical writing and the ability to influence outcomes across multidisciplinary and international stakeholder groups. Note : As part of the recruitment process, candidates will be required to complete declarations in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence. Position description: Systems Engineer - 524859.pdf To learn more about this opportunity, please contact Cameron McDonald at cameron.mcdonald@uwa.edu.au For enquiries on the recruitment process, please contact Zen Huang at zen.huang@uwa.edu.au How to apply Please apply online via the Apply Now button. The content of your Resume and Cover Letter should demonstrate how you meet the selection criteria. Closing date: 11:55 PM AWST on Sunday, 22 November 2026, with interviews likely taking place on 26 and 27 November 2026. This position is only open to applicants with relevant rights to work in Australia. Please note: Unsolicited applications from recruitment agencies will not be accepted outside of formal channels. About the University The University of Western Australia (UWA) is ranked among the top 100 universities in the world and a member of the prestigious Australian Group of Eight research intensive universities. With a strong research track record, vibrant campus and working environments, supported by the freedom to innovate and inspire, there is no better time to join Western Australia’s top university. Learn more about us. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity UWA is committed to a diverse workforce and an equitable and inclusive workplace. We are committed to fostering a safe environment for all, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, women, those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, the LGBTIQA+ community, and people living with disability. If you require any reasonable adjustments, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application. Alternatively, you can contact us for assistance during the recruitment process. If you have queries relating to your application, please contact the individual named in the advertisement. To enable a quick response, please include the 6-digit job reference number. Other jobs Lecturer - Archaeology Crawley, WA Social Sciences Join a globally connected Archaeology team and deliver hands-on field and laboratory learning in Western Australia. Helpdesk Support Assistant Crawley, WA Campus / facilities management Play a critical role as the first point of contact in a fast-paced facilities and maintenance environment. Senior Lecturer  - Regional Training Hubs (based in Broome, Derby or Kununurra) Any RCSWA site, WA. Broome, WA Health and Medical Sciences Play a key leadership role in strengthening rural medical education and training pathways across regional and remote Western Australia. Benefits Flexible working options considered. 26 weeks paid parental leave after one year and 36 weeks after five years continuous service, regardless of gender. 4 weeks annual leave with the option to purchase more. 13 weeks long service leave after seven/ten years. Salary packaging options. 17% superannuation, with the option to reduce to the minimum super guarantee. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance, and convenient on-campus childcare options. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Excluding casual positions. The University of Western Australia acknowledges that its campus is situated on Noongar land, and that Noongar people remain the spiritual and cultural custodians of their land, and continue to practise their values, languages, beliefs and knowledge. Indigenous commitment Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X Youtube Cookie Preferences Privacy Policy © 2026 The University of Western Australia Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
