    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/helpdesk-support-assistant-crawley-wa-australia": {
      "title": "Helpdesk Support Assistant",
      "description": "Helpdesk Support Assistant - Crawley, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Helpdesk Support Assistant 524761 Crawley, WA Full Time Closing on: 19 Nov 2026 Join a customer-focused team that helps keep one of Australia's leading university campuses operating efficiently and safely. Build your administration and service coordination career in a fast-paced facilities and maintenance environment. 2x full-time appointments on an ongoing basis. Base salary range: $69,666 – $77,167 p.a. (pro-rata) plus 17% superannuation. About the area Campus Management is responsible for the planning, development, management and operation of the University's physical estate and infrastructure. The team delivers integrated property, facilities, asset management, capital works and operational services that support excellence in teaching, research and campus life. Within Campus Management, the Infrastructure Maintenance team provides responsive, efficient and customer-focused support services across the University. The Helpdesk team plays a critical role as the first point of contact for maintenance requests, service enquiries and fault reporting, ensuring issues are accurately recorded, prioritised and resolved in a timely manner. About the opportunity Act as the first point of contact for service requests, maintenance enquiries and fault reporting via phone, email and customer interactions. Coordinate and monitor work orders, liaise with internal teams and contractors, and provide timely updates to stakeholders on request progress. Support operational reporting and administrative activities that contribute to effective facilities maintenance and service delivery across the University. About you Year 12 minimum or equivalent competency. Experience in delivering a high level of customer service and support. Considerable relevant administrative experience at an appropriate level Well-developed organisational skills, including the ability to meet deadlines in a busy environment. Well-developed written, verbal and interpersonal skills. Note : As part of the recruitment process, candidates will be required to complete declarations in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence. Position description: PD - Helpdesk Support Assistant (524761).pdf To learn more about this opportunity, please contact Cynthia Sandhu at cynthia.sandhu@uwa.edu.au For enquiries on the recruitment process, please contact Shelby Corrins at shelby.corrins@uwa.edu.au How to apply Please apply online via the Apply Now button. The content of your Resume and Cover Letter should demonstrate how you meet the selection criteria. Closing date: 11:55 PM AWST on Thursday, 19 November 2026 This position is only open to applicants with relevant rights to work in Australia. Please note: Unsolicited applications and emails from recruitment agencies will not be accepted outside of formal channels. Benefits Flexible working options. Generous paid leave including parental leave. Up to 17% employer paid superannuation. Salary packaging available. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance. Employee Assistance Program. About the University The University of Western Australia (UWA) is ranked among the top 100 universities in the world and a member of the prestigious Australian Group of Eight research intensive universities. With a strong research track record, vibrant campus and working environments, supported by the freedom to innovate and inspire, there is no better time to join Western Australia’s top university. Learn more about us. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity UWA is committed to a diverse workforce and an equitable and inclusive workplace. We are committed to fostering a safe environment for all, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, women, those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, the LGBTIQA+ community, and people living with disability. If you require any reasonable adjustments, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application. Alternatively, you can contact us for assistance during the recruitment process. If you have queries relating to your application, please contact the individual named in the advertisement. To enable a quick response, please include the 6-digit job reference number. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) ee23473f Last Name (required) 7ed2f106 Email (required) 445d4724 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Other jobs Lecturer - Archaeology Crawley, WA Social Sciences Join a globally connected Archaeology team and deliver hands-on field and laboratory learning in Western Australia. Systems Engineer Crawley, WA Research support, Technical/Laboratory support Design and deliver critical systems for the SKA telescope, collaborating with global experts to advance world-leading astronomy and photonics engineering Senior Lecturer  - Regional Training Hubs (based in Broome, Derby or Kununurra) Any RCSWA site, WA. Broome, WA Health and Medical Sciences Play a key leadership role in strengthening rural medical education and training pathways across regional and remote Western Australia. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 0de67b5e Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Campus / facilities management Campus / facilities management Employment Type Full Time Full Time Locations Crawley, WA, Australia Crawley, WA, Australia First Name (required) 14615be9 Last Name (required) 8e579c77 Email (required) 960f7038 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Benefits Flexible working options considered. 26 weeks paid parental leave after one year and 36 weeks after five years continuous service, regardless of gender. 4 weeks annual leave with the option to purchase more. 13 weeks long service leave after seven/ten years. Salary packaging options. 17% superannuation, with the option to reduce to the minimum super guarantee. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance, and convenient on-campus childcare options. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Excluding casual positions. The University of Western Australia acknowledges that its campus is situated on Noongar land, and that Noongar people remain the spiritual and cultural custodians of their land, and continue to practise their values, languages, beliefs and knowledge. Indigenous commitment Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X Youtube Cookie Preferences Privacy Policy © 2026 The University of Western Australia Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
