    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/senior-lecturer-regional-training-hubs-based-in-broome-derby-or-kununurra-any-rcswa-site-wa-australia-broome": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer - Regional Training Hubs (based in Broome, Derby or Kununurra)",
      "description": "Senior Lecturer  - Regional Training Hubs (based in Broome, Derby or Kununurra) - Any RCSWA site, WA, Australia - Broome, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Senior Lecturer  - Regional Training Hubs (based in Broome, Derby or Kununurra) 524848 Any RCSWA site, WA Broome, WA Part Time Closing on: 22 Nov 2026 Mentor the next generation of rural doctors while helping build a sustainable rural medical workforce Part-time (0.2 FTE) appointment on a fixed term basis for 13 months. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples. Based in a regional Western Australian community, with successful applicants required to reside in the town of appointment or the immediate surrounding area. Rural and remote allowance applies for those living in the immediate area. Clinical loading is applicable. Base salary range: Level C, $149,909– $172,441 p.a. (pro-rata) plus 17% superannuation. About the area The Rural Clinical School of Western Australia (RCSWA) is a collaborative partnership between The University of Western Australia, The University of Notre Dame Australia and Curtin University. Operating within UWA's School of Medicine, RCSWA delivers high-quality medical education, research, professional development and clinical service across rural and remote Western Australia. The Regional Training Hubs program is dedicated to strengthening rural medical training pathways and supporting medical students, junior doctors and clinicians to pursue and sustain careers in rural practice. This role offers a unique opportunity to influence workforce outcomes, improve access to healthcare in regional communities, and contribute to the future of rural medicine in Western Australia. About the opportunity Provide academic leadership in the design, coordination and delivery of innovative rural medical education, career planning and mentoring programs for medical students and junior doctors. Build and strengthen partnerships with clinicians, health services, educators and employers to expand rural training pathways, supervision capacity and career opportunities across regional and remote Western Australia. Contribute to rural health and medical education scholarship, evaluation and research while supporting statewide engagement, curriculum delivery and workforce development initiatives. About you Medical practitioner with Registration with AHPRA (or expected within 12 months of appointment) or equivalent relevant experience. Demonstrated experience supervising, teaching or mentoring medical students, junior doctors, registrars or other healthcare trainees. Strong stakeholder engagement, communication and relationship-building skills, with the ability to collaborate across health services, universities and community partners. Commitment to rural and regional healthcare, including advancing rural medical education, workforce development and positive health outcomes for rural communities. Demonstrated understanding of, and commitment to, Indigenous health, inclusion, equity and culturally responsive practice in rural and regional settings. Note : As part of the recruitment process, candidates will be required to complete declarations in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence. Position description: PD [Senior Lecturer (Regional Training Hubs)] [524848].pdf To learn more about this opportunity, please contact Robyn Fortune at robyn.fortune@rcswa.edu.au For enquiries on the recruitment process, please contact Talent Advisor at petrina.gomez@uwa.edu.au How to apply Please apply online via the Apply Now button and address the selection criteria in your submission in a separate document. For information to assist you with compiling statements to answer the selection criteria, please visit Addressing the selection criteria . You may submit a statement describing any personal circumstances relevant to your application. This can include academic/professional interruptions or achievements relative to opportunity. Closing date: 11:55 PM AWST on Sunday, 22 November 2026. The University reserves the right to shortlist and interview candidates during the advertising period. We therefore encourage you to submit your application as early as possible. This position is only open to applicants with relevant rights to work in Australia. About the University The University of Western Australia (UWA) is ranked among the top 100 universities in the world and a member of the prestigious Australian Group of Eight research intensive universities. With a strong research track record, vibrant campus and working environments, supported by the freedom to innovate and inspire, there is no better time to join Western Australia’s top university. Learn more about us. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity UWA is committed to a diverse workforce and an equitable and inclusive workplace. We are committed to fostering a safe environment for all, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, women, those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, the LGBTIQA+ community, and people living with disability. If you require any reasonable adjustments, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application. Alternatively, you can contact us for assistance during the recruitment process. If you have queries relating to your application, please contact the individual named in the advertisement. To enable a quick response, please include the 6-digit job reference number. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 5ff785eb Last Name (required) fbb908fe Email (required) 59cdd3aa Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Other jobs Lecturer - Archaeology Crawley, WA Social Sciences Join a globally connected Archaeology team and deliver hands-on field and laboratory learning in Western Australia. Systems Engineer Crawley, WA Research support, Technical/Laboratory support Design and deliver critical systems for the SKA telescope, collaborating with global experts to advance world-leading astronomy and photonics engineering Helpdesk Support Assistant Crawley, WA Campus / facilities management Play a critical role as the first point of contact in a fast-paced facilities and maintenance environment. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 71c7fcf2 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Health and Medical Sciences Health and Medical Sciences Employment Type Part Time Part Time Locations Any RCSWA site, WA, Australia Broome, WA, Australia Any RCSWA site, WA, Australia Broome, WA, Australia First Name (required) ed5512bf Last Name (required) d470757d Email (required) 0e4cd630 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Benefits Flexible working options considered. 26 weeks paid parental leave after one year and 36 weeks after five years continuous service, regardless of gender. 4 weeks annual leave with the option to purchase more. 13 weeks long service leave after seven/ten years. Salary packaging options. 17% superannuation, with the option to reduce to the minimum super guarantee. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance, and convenient on-campus childcare options. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Excluding casual positions. The University of Western Australia acknowledges that its campus is situated on Noongar land, and that Noongar people remain the spiritual and cultural custodians of their land, and continue to practise their values, languages, beliefs and knowledge. Indigenous commitment Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X Youtube Cookie Preferences Privacy Policy © 2026 The University of Western Australia Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
