    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/senior-lecturer-medical-educator-manjimup-any-rcswa-site-wa-australia-manjimup-western-australia": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer – Medical Educator (Manjimup)",
      "description": "Senior Lecturer – Medical Educator (Manjimup) - Any RCSWA site, WA, Australia - Manjimup, Western Australia, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Senior Lecturer – Medical Educator (Manjimup) 524844 Any RCSWA site, WA Manjimup, Western Australia Part Time Closing on: 22 Nov 2026 Join a collaborative academic environment where you can combine clinical education, academic leadership, community engagement and rural workforce development. Part-time (0.2 FTE), fixed-term appointment for 13 months. Based in a regional Western Australian community, with successful applicants required to reside in the town of appointment or the immediate surrounding area. Rural and remote allowance applies for those living in the immediate area. Clinical loading is applicable. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples. Base salary range: Level C, $149,909 - $172,441 p.a. (pro rata) plus 17% superannuation. About the area The Rural Clinical School of Western Australia (RCSWA) is a partnership between the University of Western Australia, The University of Notre Dame Australia and Curtin Medical School, operating within the UWA Medical School. RCSWA is a network of 15 rural and remote sites across the Kimberley, Pilbara, Mid-West, Goldfields, Great Southern and South West regions of Western Australia. Through immersive rural and remote placements, RCSWA delivers high-quality medical education, research, professional development and clinical engagement that strengthens health outcomes and supports a sustainable rural medical workforce. The School is recognised for its strong partnerships with health services, practitioners and communities across regional Western Australia. About the opportunity Lead and deliver innovative medical education, clinical teaching, mentoring and student support across rural and remote clinical settings. Coordinate high-quality clinical learning experiences through collaboration with health services, rural practitioners, community organisations, universities and key stakeholders. Contribute to curriculum development, rural health research, scholarly activity and the advancement of rural training pathways that strengthen workforce capability across regional Western Australia. About you Registered, or eligible for registration, as a Medical Practitioner with AHPRA. Demonstrated experience teaching, supervising or mentoring medical students, junior doctors and/or registrars, with a commitment to educational excellence and student success. Strong stakeholder engagement, communication and relationship-building skills, with the ability to work collaboratively across health services, universities, practitioners and communities. Commitment to rural and remote healthcare, including improving rural medical education, workforce development and health outcomes for regional communities. Demonstrated understanding of, and commitment to, Indigenous health and culturally responsive practice within rural and regional settings. Note : As part of the recruitment process, candidates will be required to complete declarations in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence. Position description: PD [Senior Lecturer, Manjimup] [524844].pdf To learn more about this opportunity, please contact Robyn Fortune at robyn.fortune@rcswa.edu.au For enquiries on the recruitment process, please contact Talent Advisor at petrina.gomez@uwa.edu.au How to apply Please apply online via the Apply Now button and address the selection criteria in your submission in a separate document. For information to assist you with compiling statements to answer the selection criteria, please visit Addressing the selection criteria . You may submit a statement describing any personal circumstances relevant to your application. This can include academic/professional interruptions or achievements relative to opportunity. Closing date: 11:55 PM AWST on Sunday, 22 November 2026. The University reserves the right to shortlist and interview candidates during the advertising period. We therefore encourage you to submit your application as early as possible. This position is only open to applicants with relevant rights to work in Australia. About the University The University of Western Australia (UWA) is ranked among the top 100 universities in the world and a member of the prestigious Australian Group of Eight research intensive universities. With a strong research track record, vibrant campus and working environments, supported by the freedom to innovate and inspire, there is no better time to join Western Australia’s top university. Learn more about us. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity UWA is committed to a diverse workforce and an equitable and inclusive workplace. We are committed to fostering a safe environment for all, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, women, those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, the LGBTIQA+ community, and people living with disability. If you require any reasonable adjustments, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application. Alternatively, you can contact us for assistance during the recruitment process. If you have queries relating to your application, please contact the individual named in the advertisement. To enable a quick response, please include the 6-digit job reference number. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) fcbd90de Last Name (required) 3c64a846 Email (required) f164224e Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Other jobs Lecturer - Archaeology Crawley, WA Social Sciences Join a globally connected Archaeology team and deliver hands-on field and laboratory learning in Western Australia. Systems Engineer Crawley, WA Research support, Technical/Laboratory support Design and deliver critical systems for the SKA telescope, collaborating with global experts to advance world-leading astronomy and photonics engineering Helpdesk Support Assistant Crawley, WA Campus / facilities management Play a critical role as the first point of contact in a fast-paced facilities and maintenance environment. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 0c4db8a4 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Health and Medical Sciences Health and Medical Sciences Employment Type Part Time Part Time Locations Any RCSWA site, WA, Australia Manjimup, Western Australia, Australia Any RCSWA site, WA, Australia Manjimup, Western Australia, Australia First Name (required) 8065c587 Last Name (required) 8b665210 Email (required) 16a5510d Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Benefits Flexible working options considered. 26 weeks paid parental leave after one year and 36 weeks after five years continuous service, regardless of gender. 4 weeks annual leave with the option to purchase more. 13 weeks long service leave after seven/ten years. Salary packaging options. 17% superannuation, with the option to reduce to the minimum super guarantee. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance, and convenient on-campus childcare options. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Excluding casual positions. The University of Western Australia acknowledges that its campus is situated on Noongar land, and that Noongar people remain the spiritual and cultural custodians of their land, and continue to practise their values, languages, beliefs and knowledge. Indigenous commitment Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X Youtube Cookie Preferences Privacy Policy © 2026 The University of Western Australia Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improv