      "description": "Senior Lecturer – Medical Educator (Broome) - Broome, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Senior Lecturer – Medical Educator (Broome) 524838 Broome, WA Part Time Closing on: 22 Nov 2026 Join a collaborative academic environment where you can combine clinical education, academic leadership, community engagement and rural workforce development. Part-time (0.4 FTE), fixed-term appointment for 2 years. Based in a regional Western Australian community, with successful applicants required to reside in the town of appointment or the immediate surrounding area. Rural and remote allowance applies for those living in the immediate area. Clinical loading is applicable. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples. Base salary range: Level C, $149,909 - $172,441 p.a. (pro rata) plus 17% superannuation. About the area The Rural Clinical School of Western Australia (RCSWA) is a partnership between the University of Western Australia, The University of Notre Dame Australia and Curtin Medical School, operating within the UWA Medical School. RCSWA is a network of 15 rural and remote sites across the Kimberley, Pilbara, Mid-West, Goldfields, Great Southern and South West regions of Western Australia. Through immersive rural and remote placements, RCSWA delivers high-quality medical education, research, professional development and clinical engagement that strengthens health outcomes and supports a sustainable rural medical workforce. The School is recognised for its strong partnerships with health services, practitioners and communities across regional Western Australia. About the opportunity Lead and deliver innovative medical education, clinical teaching, mentoring and student support across rural and remote clinical settings. Coordinate high-quality clinical learning experiences through collaboration with health services, rural practitioners, community organisations, universities and key stakeholders. Contribute to curriculum development, rural health research, scholarly activity and the advancement of rural training pathways that strengthen workforce capability across regional Western Australia. About you Registered, or eligible for registration, as a Medical Practitioner with AHPRA. Demonstrated experience teaching, supervising or mentoring medical students, junior doctors and/or registrars, with a commitment to educational excellence and student success. Strong stakeholder engagement, communication and relationship-building skills, with the ability to work collaboratively across health services, universities, practitioners and communities. Commitment to rural and remote healthcare, including improving rural medical education, workforce development and health outcomes for regional communities. Demonstrated understanding of, and commitment to, Indigenous health and culturally responsive practice within rural and regional settings. Note : As part of the recruitment process, candidates will be required to complete declarations in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence. Position description: PD [Senior Lecturer – Medical Educator (Broome)] [524838].pdf To learn more about this opportunity, please contact Robyn Fortune at robyn.fortune@rcswa.edu.au For enquiries on the recruitment process, please contact Talent Advisor at petrina.gomez@uwa.edu.au How to apply Please apply online via the Apply Now button and address the selection criteria in your submission in a separate document. For information to assist you with compiling statements to answer the selection criteria, please visit Addressing the selection criteria . You may submit a statement describing any personal circumstances relevant to your application. This can include academic/professional interruptions or achievements relative to opportunity. Closing date: 11:55 PM AWST on Sunday, 22 November 2026. The University reserves t