    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/communications-officer-crawley-wa-australia": {
      "title": "Communications Officer",
      "description": "Communications Officer - Crawley, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Communications Officer 524690 Crawley, WA Part Time Closing on: 18 Nov 2026 Lead strategic communications for one of the world’s longest-running and most comprehensive longitudinal health studies. Translate high-impact research into clear, engaging stories for participants, partners, researchers and the wider community. Part-time (0.6 FTE) appointment on a fixed term basis for 24 months. Base salary range: $108,413 – $120,287 p.a. (pro-rata) plus 17% superannuation. About the area The Raine Study is one of the world’s longest-running and most comprehensive longitudinal health research studies. Established in Western Australia in 1989, it follows participants and their families across multiple generations to understand how genetic, environmental, lifestyle and social factors shape health and wellbeing across the life course. Hosted by UWA’s School of Population and Global Health, the Raine Study is supported by a collaborative partnership of leading Western Australian universities and research institutes. You will join a multidisciplinary team that sustains a globally recognised research resource and helps turn research findings into better clinical practice, public health policy and outcomes for current and future generations. About the opportunity Develop and implement a communications plan for the Raine Study, across traditional media, social media, websites, newsletters, campaigns and promotional channels, ensuring clear, consistent messaging and brand alignment. Create accessible written, visual and multimedia content that communicates research outcomes, organisational achievements, events and participant engagement activities to diverse audiences. Partner with Directors, researchers, internal teams and joint venture communications specialists to identify media and storytelling opportunities, strengthen stakeholder engagement, and monitor and report on communications performance. About you A relevant tertiary qualification with at least four years’ subsequent experience, extensive demonstrated communications expertise, or an equivalent combination of education, training and experience. Substantial experience in strategic communications, public relations, marketing or advertising, ideally within health, science, research or another complex stakeholder environment. Excellent writing and editing skills, with the ability to translate complex or scientific information into accurate, audience-focused content across digital, print and promotional channels. Demonstrated capability managing websites, newsletters and social media, using audience insights and performance measures to improve engagement and reach. Strong stakeholder management, interpersonal, organisational and problem-solving skills; experience with Canva or Adobe Creative Suite, photography, video production or editing will be highly regarded. Note : As part of the recruitment process, candidates will be required to complete declarations in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence. A current National Police Clearance and “C” class driver’s licence will be required by the successful applicant. Position description: PD - Communications Officer (524690).pdf To learn more about this opportunity, please contact Aggie Bouckley at aggie.bouckley@uwa.edu.au For enquiries on the recruitment process, please contact Pratik Sridhar at pratik.sridhar@uwa.edu.au How to apply Please apply online via the Apply Now button. The content of your Resume and Cover Letter should demonstrate how you meet the selection criteria. Closing date: 11:55 PM AWST on Wednesday 18 November 2026 This position is only open to applicants with relevant rights to work in Australia. Please note: Unsolicited applications from recruitment agencies will not be accepted outside of formal channels. Benefits Flexible working options. Generous paid leave including parental leave. Up to 17% employer paid superannuation. Salary packaging available. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance. Employee Assistance Program. About the University The University of Western Australia (UWA) is ranked among the top 100 universities in the world and a member of the prestigious Australian Group of Eight research intensive universities. With a strong research track record, vibrant campus and working environments, supported by the freedom to innovate and inspire, there is no better time to join Western Australia’s top university. Learn more about us. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity UWA is committed to a diverse workforce and an equitable and inclusive workplace. We are committed to fostering a safe environment for all, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, women, those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, the LGBTIQA+ community, and people living with disability. If you require any reasonable adjustments, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application. Alternatively, you can contact us for assistance during the recruitment process. If you have queries relating to your application, please contact the individual named in the advertisement. To enable a quick response, please include the 6-digit job reference number. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 94159521 Last Name (required) 54547865 Email (required) 37941f8a Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Other jobs Lecturer - Archaeology Crawley, WA Social Sciences Join a globally connected Archaeology team and deliver hands-on field and laboratory learning in Western Australia. Systems Engineer Crawley, WA Research support, Technical/Laboratory support Design and deliver critical systems for the SKA telescope, collaborating with global experts to advance world-leading astronomy and photonics engineering Helpdesk Support Assistant Crawley, WA Campus / facilities management Play a critical role as the first point of contact in a fast-paced facilities and maintenance environment. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 4894f47a Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Community Engagement/Marketing Community Engagement/Marketing Employment Type Part Time Part Time Locations Crawley, WA, Australia Crawley, WA, Australia First Name (required) 770e49ec Last Name (required) 4e2ef078 Email (required) 41fe8815 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Benefits Flexible working options considered. 26 weeks paid parental leave after one year and 36 weeks after five years continuous service, regardless of gender. 4 weeks annual leave with the option to purchase more. 13 weeks long service leave after seven/ten years. Salary packaging options. 17% superannuation, with the option to reduce to the minimum super guarantee. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance, and convenient on-campus childcare options. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Excluding casual positions. The University of Western Australia acknowledges that its campus is situated on Noongar land, and that Noongar people remain the spiritual and cultural custodians of their land, and continue to practise their values, languages, beliefs and knowledge. Indigenous commitment Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X Youtube Cookie Preferences Privacy Policy © 2026 The University of Western Australia Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
