    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/lecturer-medical-education-crawley-wa-australia": {
      "title": "Lecturer – Medical Education",
      "description": "Lecturer – Medical Education - Crawley, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Lecturer – Medical Education 524427 Crawley, WA Part Time Closing on: 11 Nov 2026 Coordinate and deliver Medical Education Micro-Credentials across clinical teaching, simulation, mentoring and assessment. Part-time (7.5 hours a fortnight) appointment on a fixed term basis until 31 December 2027. Base salary range: Level B, $122,876 – $145,404 p.a. (pro-rata) plus 17% superannuation. About the area The UWA Medical School is Western Australia’s largest and longest-established medical school. It delivers a four-year postgraduate medical program to local, national and international students and supports substantial research across a broad range of medical disciplines. Within the School, the MD Educational Unit supports high-quality learning, teaching and assessment. This role contributes to the Med Ed Greenhouse program, which connects doctors-in-training with medical education development and teaching opportunities. About the opportunity Coordinate the suite of Medical Education Micro-Credentials offered through the Med Ed Greenhouse program. Deliver and assess the Clinical Teaching in Medical Education micro-credential and support delivery and assessment across simulation, mentoring and assessment offerings. Build supportive relationships with doctors-in-training, connect participants with teaching and content-development opportunities, and contribute to program administration, accreditation and continuous improvement. About you Medical practitioner with current AHPRA registration who is working, or able to work, in a Western Australian teaching hospital. Demonstrated experience delivering clinical teaching and assessment across teaching activities, units or courses, informed by contemporary medical education evidence. Strong relationship-building and communication skills, with the ability to engage academic staff, students, doctors-in-training, junior doctor societies and postgraduate medical education teams. Confidence using digital learning and collaboration platforms, including learning management systems and Microsoft Teams, together with a commitment to inclusive teaching and learner support. A postgraduate qualification in health professions education, or equivalent experience, and experience in medical education at medical student, prevocational or specialty training level will be highly regarded. Note : As part of the recruitment process, candidates will be required to complete declarations in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence. Position description: PD - Lecturer (524427).pdf To learn more about this opportunity, please contact Kate Jutsum at kate.jutsum@uwa.edu.au For enquiries on the recruitment process, please contact Petrina Gomez at petrina.gomez@uwa.edu.au How to apply Please apply online via the Apply Now button and address the selection criteria in your submission in a separate document. For information to assist you with compiling statements to answer the selection criteria, please visit Addressing the selection criteria . You may submit a statement describing any personal circumstances relevant to your application. This can include academic/professional interruptions or achievements relative to opportunity. Closing date: 11:55 PM AWST on Wednesday, 11 November 2026 This position is only open to applicants with relevant rights to work in Australia. About the University The University of Western Australia (UWA) is ranked among the top 100 universities in the world and a member of the prestigious Australian Group of Eight research intensive universities. With a strong research track record, vibrant campus and working environments, supported by the freedom to innovate and inspire, there is no better time to join Western Australia’s top university. Learn more about us. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity UWA is committed to a diverse workforce and an equitable and inclusive workplace. We are committed to fostering a safe environment for all, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, women, those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, the LGBTIQA+ community, and people living with disability. If you require any reasonable adjustments, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application. Alternatively, you can contact us for assistance during the recruitment process. If you have queries relating to your application, please contact the individual named in the advertisement. To enable a quick response, please include the 6-digit job reference number. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 3560aa60 Last Name (required) a1260981 Email (required) c8ec65db Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Other jobs Lecturer - Archaeology Crawley, WA Social Sciences Join a globally connected Archaeology team and deliver hands-on field and laboratory learning in Western Australia. Systems Engineer Crawley, WA Research support, Technical/Laboratory support Design and deliver critical systems for the SKA telescope, collaborating with global experts to advance world-leading astronomy and photonics engineering Helpdesk Support Assistant Crawley, WA Campus / facilities management Play a critical role as the first point of contact in a fast-paced facilities and maintenance environment. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert db4a2019 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Health and Medical Sciences Health and Medical Sciences Employment Type Part Time Part Time Locations Crawley, WA, Australia Crawley, WA, Australia First Name (required) 2d796f0b Last Name (required) 4c504502 Email (required) e434d20a Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Benefits Flexible working options considered. 26 weeks paid parental leave after one year and 36 weeks after five years continuous service, regardless of gender. 4 weeks annual leave with the option to purchase more. 13 weeks long service leave after seven/ten years. Salary packaging options. 17% superannuation, with the option to reduce to the minimum super guarantee. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance, and convenient on-campus childcare options. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Excluding casual positions. The University of Western Australia acknowledges that its campus is situated on Noongar land, and that Noongar people remain the spiritual and cultural custodians of their land, and continue to practise their values, languages, beliefs and knowledge. Indigenous commitment Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X Youtube Cookie Preferences Privacy Policy © 2026 The University of Western Australia Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
