    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/technical-officer-crawley-wa-australia-a7dedc38-591c-4bc3-9fb8-4e78f6c5ffdb": {
      "title": "Technical Officer",
      "description": "Technical Officer - Crawley, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Technical Officer 524789 Crawley, WA Full Time Closing on: 25 Nov 2026 Help deliver nationally significant coastal and marine research across WA. Get hands-on with marine fieldwork, equipment and research data. Full-time appointment on a fixed term basis for 2 years. Base salary range: $86,540 – $95,920 p.a. (pro-rata) plus 17% superannuation. About the area The School of Earth and Oceans undertakes fundamental and applied coastal and marine research at an internationally recognised standard. Ocean-focused staff and research infrastructure are located at the Indian Ocean Marine Research Centre in Crawley and the Coastal and Offshore Research Laboratory in Shenton Park. The School delivers field-based research across coastal and offshore environments. This includes the Integrated Marine Observing System (IMOS) Coastal Wave Buoy Facility and the Western Australian node of the National Coastal Observing Facility (NCOF), supported through the Australian Government's National Collaborative Research Infrastructure Strategy as part of the CoastRI program. The resulting national observing network helps researchers and end users understand coastal processes and anticipate changes affecting habitats, industries and communities. About the opportunity Prepare, test, organise and maintain oceanographic instruments, marine field equipment, and bathymetric and topographic survey systems for coastal research programs. Support the planning and safe delivery of marine fieldwork from small vessels, including boating and diving activities, field logistics and OHS risk assessments. Process, quality-control, analyse, archive and present field datasets, and contribute to technical reports, publications, training and equipment inductions. About you A degree in coastal science, marine science or a related discipline, or equivalent relevant industry experience. Experience supporting coastal field research or industry projects, ideally involving marine field instrumentation and small-vessel operations. Strong organisational skills, with the ability to prioritise work, solve practical problems and contribute both independently and as part of a team. Well-developed written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to explain technical information and contribute to reports. Computing capability across spreadsheets and databases, with experience in, or willingness to learn, tools such as MATLAB, Python, R, ArcGIS, Agisoft Metashape or SBG Qinertia. Qualifications in small-vessel operations, scientific diving, UAV/GNSS surveying or forklift operation, or willingness to obtain them, will be highly regarded. Note : As part of the recruitment process, candidates will be required to complete declarations in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence. A current “C” class driver’s licence will be required by the successful applicant. Position description: PD - Technical Officer (524789).pdf To learn more about this opportunity, please contact Mike Cuttler at michael.cuttler@uwa.edu.au For enquiries on the recruitment process, please contact Maddy Chaplin at maddy.chaplin@uwa.edu.au How to apply Please apply online via the Apply Now button. The content of your Resume and Cover Letter should demonstrate how you meet the selection criteria. Closing date: 11:55 PM AWST on Wednesday, 25 November 2026. This position is only open to applicants with relevant rights to work in Australia. Please note: Unsolicited applications from recruitment agencies will not be accepted outside of formal channels. Benefits Flexible working options. Generous paid leave including parental leave. Up to 17% employer paid superannuation. Salary packaging available. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance. Employee Assistance Program. About the University The University of Western Australia (UWA) is ranked among the top 100 universities in the world and a member of the prestigious Australian Group of Eight research intensive universities. With a strong research track record, vibrant campus and working environments, supported by the freedom to innovate and inspire, there is no better time to join Western Australia’s top university. Learn more about us. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity UWA is committed to a diverse workforce and an equitable and inclusive workplace. We are committed to fostering a safe environment for all, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, women, those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, the LGBTIQA+ community, and people living with disability. If you require any reasonable adjustments, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application. Alternatively, you can contact us for assistance during the recruitment process. If you have queries relating to your application, please contact the individual named in the advertisement. To enable a quick response, please include the 6-digit job reference number. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) b4756db5 Last Name (required) b1465196 Email (required) 6365157b Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Other jobs Lecturer - Archaeology Crawley, WA Social Sciences Join a globally connected Archaeology team and deliver hands-on field and laboratory learning in Western Australia. Systems Engineer Crawley, WA Research support, Technical/Laboratory support Design and deliver critical systems for the SKA telescope, collaborating with global experts to advance world-leading astronomy and photonics engineering Helpdesk Support Assistant Crawley, WA Campus / facilities management Play a critical role as the first point of contact in a fast-paced facilities and maintenance environment. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 47f70190 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Technical/Laboratory support Technical/Laboratory support Employment Type Full Time Full Time Locations Crawley, WA, Australia Crawley, WA, Australia First Name (required) 663a1fb1 Last Name (required) f3e0ba82 Email (required) 5684d822 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Benefits Flexible working options considered. 26 weeks paid parental leave after one year and 36 weeks after five years continuous service, regardless of gender. 4 weeks annual leave with the option to purchase more. 13 weeks long service leave after seven/ten years. Salary packaging options. 17% superannuation, with the option to reduce to the minimum super guarantee. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance, and convenient on-campus childcare options. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Excluding casual positions. The University of Western Australia acknowledges that its campus is situated on Noongar land, and that Noongar people remain the spiritual and cultural custodians of their land, and continue to practise their values, languages, beliefs and knowledge. Indigenous commitment Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X Youtube Cookie Preferences Privacy Policy © 2026 The University of Western Australia Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
