    "https://external.jobs.uwa.edu.au/jobs/academic-services-officer-kalgoorlie-kalgoorlie-wa-australia": {
      "title": "Academic Services Officer - Kalgoorlie",
      "description": "Academic Services Officer - Kalgoorlie - Kalgoorlie, WA, Australia Back to UWA My Profile Kiosk mode Pause the proceeding carousel Academic Services Officer - Kalgoorlie 524746 Kalgoorlie, WA Full Time Closing on: 15 Nov 2026 Make a meaningful contribution to improving health outcomes in rural and remote communities through high-quality student and academic support. You must reside in the town of appointment or the immediate surrounding area. District Allowance applied to those living in the immediate area. We strongly encourage applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples. Full-time appointment on fixed term basis for 2 years. Base salary range: $86,540– $95,920 p.a. (pro-rata) plus 17% superannuation. About the area The Academic Services team provides high-quality administrative and academic support services to students, academic staff and professional staff across the University, with a strong focus on service excellence, collaboration and continuous improvement. The Rural Clinical School of Western Australia (RCSWA), part of the UWA Medical School, delivers rural clinical training for medical students from The University of Western Australia, Curtin University and The University of Notre Dame Australia. Operating across a network spanning more than 3,500 kilometres throughout Western Australia, RCSWA plays a vital role in developing the rural medical workforce and improving health outcomes in rural and remote communities. About the opportunity Coordinate and deliver a broad range of administrative and logistical services that support the successful delivery of rural medical student placement programs. Provide high-quality advice and support to students, staff and external stakeholders, responding to complex enquiries with initiative, judgement and a customer-focused approach. Contribute to continuous improvement by enhancing administrative processes, systems and workflows that support effective program delivery and the student experience. About you Relevant tertiary qualification or an equivalent combination of education, training and administrative experience. Demonstrated experience providing high-level administrative support in a complex, service-oriented environment. Strong organisational and time management skills, with the ability to manage competing priorities, work independently and meet deadlines. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to build productive relationships with colleagues, students and external stakeholders. Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications and business systems, together with a commitment to teamwork, continuous improvement and quality service delivery. Note : As part of the recruitment process, candidates will be required to complete declarations in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence. Position description: PD [Academic Services Officer] [524746].pdf To learn more about this opportunity, please contact Robyn Fortune at robyn.fortune@rcswa.edu.au For enquiries on the recruitment process, please contact Talent Advisor at petrina.gomez@uwa.edu.au How to apply Please apply online via the Apply Now button. The content of your Resume and Cover Letter should demonstrate how you meet the selection criteria. Closing date: 11:55 PM AWST on Sunday, 15 November 2026. This position is only open to applicants with relevant rights to work in Australia. Please note: Unsolicited applications from recruitment agencies will not be accepted outside of formal channels. About the University The University of Western Australia (UWA) is ranked among the top 100 universities in the world and a member of the prestigious Australian Group of Eight research intensive universities. With a strong research track record, vibrant campus and working environments, supported by the freedom to innovate and inspire, there is no better time to join Western Australia’s top university. Learn more about us. Our commitment to inclusion and diversity UWA is committed to a diverse workforce and an equitable and inclusive workplace. We are committed to fostering a safe environment for all, including Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people, women, those from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds, the LGBTIQA+ community, and people living with disability. If you require any reasonable adjustments, we encourage you to advise us at the time of application. Alternatively, you can contact us for assistance during the recruitment process. If you have queries relating to your application, please contact the individual named in the advertisement. To enable a quick response, please include the 6-digit job reference number. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) c7e090cd Last Name (required) ff403047 Email (required) aa55d83f Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Other jobs Lecturer - Archaeology Crawley, WA Social Sciences Join a globally connected Archaeology team and deliver hands-on field and laboratory learning in Western Australia. Systems Engineer Crawley, WA Research support, Technical/Laboratory support Design and deliver critical systems for the SKA telescope, collaborating with global experts to advance world-leading astronomy and photonics engineering Helpdesk Support Assistant Crawley, WA Campus / facilities management Play a critical role as the first point of contact in a fast-paced facilities and maintenance environment. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert b5a91b7d Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Administration & Executive support Administration & Executive support Employment Type Full Time Full Time Locations Kalgoorlie, WA, Australia Kalgoorlie, WA, Australia First Name (required) 1860399e Last Name (required) fd93a005 Email (required) d3f285ad Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Benefits Flexible working options considered. 26 weeks paid parental leave after one year and 36 weeks after five years continuous service, regardless of gender. 4 weeks annual leave with the option to purchase more. 13 weeks long service leave after seven/ten years. Salary packaging options. 17% superannuation, with the option to reduce to the minimum super guarantee. Up to 25% discount on eligible UWA full-fee courses. Discounted health insurance, and convenient on-campus childcare options. Incremental progression based on 12 months continuous service. Excluding casual positions. The University of Western Australia acknowledges that its campus is situated on Noongar land, and that Noongar people remain the spiritual and cultural custodians of their land, and continue to practise their values, languages, beliefs and knowledge. Indigenous commitment Facebook Instagram LinkedIn X Youtube Cookie Preferences Privacy Policy © 2026 The University of Western Australia Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
